SUMMARY:Mt. Mitchell to Winter Star\, 8.4mi\, 2\,900ft\, Fitness Hike
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\n8:45 for carpooling at the Bull Cr
 eek Valley Overlook on the Parkway OR 9:30 at the Mt. Mitchell picnic area
 /Black Mountain Crest Trailhead. ...If you sign up and change your mind ev
 en if on a waitlist\, change your RSVP to "not attending" to free up your 
 reservation.\n\nOut and back: We will hike the Black Mountain Crest from t
 he picnic area (lower parking lot) to Winter Star Mountain and back. Gorge
 ous vistas await.\n\nPACE: All fitness hikes have a brisk steady pace (\\~
 3 mi/hr)\, adjusting for trail conditions\, and regrouping as needed. Thes
 e hikes are specifically for conditioned hikers. Please be sure of your hi
 king ability before signing on. This hike includes some rock\, rope\, and 
 ladder climbing.\n\nCAR POOL: For those who wish to car pool\, we will mee
 t at the Bull Creek Valley Overlook on the Parkway. Tell the hike leader w
 here you intend to meet the group: Bull Creek Overlook (8:45am) or Mt. Mit
 chell picnic area trailhead (9:30).\n\nDriving to Mt. Mitchell picnic area
 : From Asheville\, take the Blue Ridge Parkway north/east past the various
  Craggies to Route 128. Turn left toward Mt. Mitchell. Drive all the way t
 o the Mt. Mitchell parking lot. The picnic area is to your left just as yo
 u enter the parking lot on the lower level.\n\nDogs are welcome\, but have
  a leash handy for walking through the picnic area and later\, in case we 
 run into other hikers or dogs.\n\nHIKE LEVELS are based on the total eleva
 tion gain for each hike while distances vary as described. Lower level hik
 es focus on endurance conditioning and higher-level hikes add increasing c
 ardio challenges. This one is level 9.\n\nHike Level (1) Up to 600 feet of
  elevation gain. Level (2) 600'- 900'\; Level (3) 900' - 1200'\; Level (4)
  1200' - 1500'\; Level (5) 1\,500' - 1\,800'\; Level (6) 1\,800' - 2\,100'
 \; Level (7) 2\,100' - 2\,400'\; Level (8) 2\,400' - 2700'\; Level (9) 270
 0' - 3000' Level (10) 3000' - 4000'\; ULTIMATE HIKES are hikes > 4\,000' e
 levation gain\; We post 3-4 of these hike challenges a year.\n\n**Release 
 of Liability:**\nThe organizer of this trip is a volunteer and not a profe
 ssional guide. The function of the organizer is only to organize this trip
 . If you sign up or participate in this event you acknowledge that you fre
 ely and voluntarily agree to assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, an
 d damages arising from\, as a result of\, and associated with this event. 
 In addition\, you acknowledge that you agree to the Meetup terms: https://
 www.meetup.com/terms
